KiB; required strings (paths, `role: license-review`, `attempt: 1`, `UNTRUSTED`, five severities, `At most 50 findings`, `$ARD_ROLE_DIR/allowlist.txt`, `$ARD_SIDECAR/licenses/allowlist.txt`, the go-licenses commands, `go mod download -json`, `package-lock.json`, `## Checks`, `## Dependencies`, `No dependency changes to review`); no banned strings; `redact.Builtin().Scan` finds nothing.\n- `TestLicenseReviewPromptExamples`: every example parses with `closeout.Parse`; role and attempt right, no `next` or `worker`; verdict matches blocking; `closeout.Build` gives changes, done or needs-human labels; coverage of all four outcome kinds; a `go.mod` finding and a `package-lock.json` finding; each `changes` example mentions \"allowlist\".\n- `TestLicenseAllowlist`: lines match the SPDX regex, no duplicates, sorted, no trailing whitespace, contains MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-3-Clause, and none of GPL-, AGPL-, LGPL-, SSPL-, BUSL-, CC-BY-NC.\n- Updated `TestFSContents`, `TestEmbeddedEngReviewLoadsAsReviewer` and initcmd `TestInitOpensPR` still pass.\n- Failure and edge cases: an empty allowlist example is needs-human; WITH-expression regex case; integration blocks on non-allowlisted MIT and passes when listed.\n- Manual smoke test on a scratch repo and adding the role to ard's own `.ard/` are human follow-ups.\n\n### Risk\n\nLow. New embedded files and tests only, no controller code. Protected paths touched: `CLAUDE.md` only (needs human merge approval); `.ard/` and `.github/` are untouched. Security-sensitive: the prompt must keep the allowlist owner-controlled and treat manifests and LICENSE text as untrusted. The embedded tree changes what `ard init` proposes. The role runs as a host subprocess (#84 warning). Merge conflicts with #43 on shared lists are likely but trivial.\n\n### Size\n\nM. Files: `internal/roles/reviewers/license-review/{prompt.txt,allowlist.txt}`, `internal/roles/{config.yaml,roles.go,roles_test.go,eng_review_test.go,license_review_test.go,license_review_integration_test.go}`, `internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go`, `docs/proposal.md`, `CLAUDE.md`.\ninternal/roles/config.yaml\ninternal/roles/cve_docker_integration_test.go\ninternal/roles/cve_integration_test.go\ninternal/roles/cve_test.go\ninternal/roles/eng_review_test.go\ninternal/roles/engineer_test.go\ninternal/roles/errcodes_integration_test.go\ninternal/roles/errcodes_test.go\ninternal/roles/lead_test.go\ninternal/roles/roles.go\ninternal/roles/roles_test.go\ninternal/roles/worker_engineer_test.go\n\ninternal/roles:\nconfig.yaml\ncve_docker_integration_test.go\ncve_integration_test.go\ncve_test.go\neng_review_test.go\nengineer_test.go\nerrcodes_integration_test.go\nerrcodes_test.go\nlead_test.go\nreviewers\nroles.go\nroles_test.go\nscanners\ntestdata\ntriage\nworker_engineer_test.go\nworkers\n\ninternal/roles/reviewers:\neng-review\n\ninternal/roles/scanners:\ncve\nerror-codes\n\ninternal/roles/testdata:\ncve\n\ninternal/roles/triage:\nengineer\nlead\n\ninternal/roles/workers:\nengineer\nea9d4d0 ard(triage:engineer): #215 Adds a scanner `route` key (config schema, validation, and label handli… [skip ci]\ndbfde15 ard(triage:lead): #43 The revised issue now asks only for a starter security reviewer that sh… [skip ci]\nd94ea99 ard(triage:engineer): #222 Rewrites the three credentialed-URL test fixtures to build them at run… [skip ci]\nb80b330 Add plan for #43: starter security-review reviewer role (#226)\n2234113 ard(triage:engineer): #61 Adds a new janitor loop in its own package that finds closed issues pas… [skip ci]\nebd120f ard(triage:lead): #221 The request is a clear change: post one notice per scanner failure stre… [skip ci]\ncad2860 ard(triage:lead): #222 A test-only change: three existing tests in separate internal packages… [skip ci]\n11a050b ard(triage:engineer): #44 Adds a starter license-review reviewer to the embedded roles: a prompt,… [skip ci]\n4cbd42c ard(triage:lead): #58 The daily digest is a clear change, but one of its four required figure… [skip ci]\