{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EU9SnsAJBbadzXfVdenrMC","type":"tool_result","content":"  scanners/cve:             { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/error-codes:     { every: 24h, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/lint:            { every: 24h, max_open: 3, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n  triage/lead:              { sidecar: vpe-specs, timeout: 15m, model: claude-opus-5-5 }\n  triage/architect:         { sidecar: vpe-specs }\n  triage/engineer:          { after: [architect, product-manager, designer, documentation-planner] }\n  workers/engineer:         { tests: make test, timeout: 60m, reviewers: [security-review, eng-review] }\n  reviewers/license-review: { agent: kimi, when: { paths: [\"**/go.mod\", \"**/go.sum\", \"**/package*.json\"] } }\n  reviewers/web-review: { when: { paths: [web/] } }\n```\n\n**The label is the gate, not GitHub's \"request changes\".** A bot's request-changes review blocks merge until someone dismisses it, even after the fix. Reviews post as comments; `ard:review:<role>:changes` is what sends the PR back to the worker.\n\n**Pair each reviewer with a deterministic tool where one exists.** The tool finds; the agent explains, ranks and checks the result against the plan.\n\n| Reviewer | Runs when | Deterministic aid | Blocks on |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| security-review | always | semgrep or gosec, secret scan | injection, authz gaps, secrets, unsafe dependencies |\n| eng-review | always | lint and coverage of added lines (the repo's own commands, run by the agent) | correctness, missing tests, drift from `plan.md` |\n| license-review | a manifest or lockfile changes | go-licenses or scancode | a license outside the allowlist |\n| product-manager-review | the issue had PM triage, or UI paths change | none | acceptance criteria not met |\n\n116:**Who may write what.** Close-out checks every changed file under `.ard/<issue#>/` against the job's allowlist:\n127:A worker's inputs are `.ard-input/<issue#>/issue.md`, `comments.md` and, on a fix step, `test-output.log` (written by the loop, never committed) and `.ard/<issue#>/plan.md`. Nobody may change `issue.md` (only the sca\n129:Close-out checks `plan.md` against the job's base commit, but the committer writes it onto the latest `main`. So at commit time the committer replaces only the job's own `##` section in the current `main` copy (addin\n202:| cve | osv-scanner and govulncheck (trivy and the Dependabot alerts API later) | 6 h | 1 | yes |\n211:**The cve scanner** (`scanners/cve`, a `sh` script plus one `jq` program, no build step) merges osv-scanner (all ecosystems) and govulncheck (Go reachability). Its fingerprint is `osv:<advisory>:<manifest>:<package>`\n277:**The agent's contract is narrow.** It may edit files in its worktree and must write `.ard/<issue#>/<stage>-<role>.md` with a `status`. Under `.ard/<issue#>/` it may change only its own role file and what its role's \n279:**Close-out is resumable.** The controller (`internal/closeout`) decides the outcome from the role file (only one this job wrote), stages the redacted files, then commits, requests the `next` labels, posts one summar\n322:3. **Run the agent** with `.ard/reviewers/<role>/prompt.txt` and these untrusted inputs: `.ard-input/<issue#>/diff.patch` (the controller's diff from the merge base with `main` to the pinned head, `--stat` then the p\n338:| license-review | a manifest or lockfile changes | go-licenses or scancode | a license outside the allowlist |\n384:- Any other file in the directory (scripts, allowlists) is mounted read-only beside the prompt.\n93:\tPaths  []string // run only when the diff touches one of these paths\n169:\tProtectedPaths []string // merge.protected_paths: \"dir/\" = directory prefix, else doublestar glob; see Protected\n244:// otherwise it does when any changed path matches any Paths entry, or any\n250:// means the changed paths are unknown: a rule with