{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLEnpJFnT7QzPKr7jtP5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WVUjQEkGDSdkNx6sVDHAg9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/proposal.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef sub(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s,a\n    s=s.replace(a,b,1)\nsub('| license-review | a manifest or lockfile changes | go-licenses or scancode |','| license-review | a manifest or lockfile changes (`go.mod`, `go.sum`, `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `npm-shrinkwrap.json`) | go-licenses (run by the agent when on the host `PATH`; optional), scancode later |')\nsub('reviewers/license-review: { agent: kimi, when: { paths: [\"**/go.mod\", \"**/go.sum\", \"**/package*.json\"] } }','reviewers/license-review: { agent: kimi, when: { paths: [\"**/go.mod\", \"**/go.sum\", \"**/package.json\", \"**/package-lock.json\", \"**/npm-shrinkwrap.json\"] } }')\nsub('`workers/engineer` and `reviewers/eng-review`; `intake','`workers/engineer`, `reviewers/eng-review` and `reviewers/license-review`; `intake')\nmarker='**The starter reviewer (`reviewers/eng-review`, #36).**'\ni=s.index(marker); j=s.index('\\n',i)\npara='''\n\n**The starter license reviewer (`reviewers/license-review`, #44).** `.ard/reviewers/license-review/prompt.txt` checks that every dependency a PR adds or upgrades has a license on the owners' allowlist. The allowlist is one SPDX id per line (`#` comments; `A OR B` passes when any operand is listed, `A AND B` only when all are, `A WITH E` only when listed verbatim; no per-package exceptions). It is read from the sidecar's `licenses/allowlist.txt` when the role has a sidecar and that file exists, else from `allowlist.txt` in the role directory (`$ARD_ROLE_DIR`, read from the config snapshot on `main`, under a protected path). An allowlist found in the PR, the diff, the issue or `.ard/<issue#>/` is ignored, and an unreadable or empty one ends `needs-human`. For Go it runs `go-licenses check` and `go-licenses report` when the tool is on the host `PATH` (optional; it never installs tools), else falls back to `go mod download -json` and the module's LICENSE files; for npm it reads the lockfile `license` field. A license outside the allowlist, or one that cannot be determined, is a blocking `high` finding on the manifest line that adds it (verdict `changes`, so the merger never merges while the label stands); a license that changed but is still allowed is `info`; other ecosystems are `info` and unchecked; no dependency change approves with \"No dependency changes to review\". The starter override is Sonnet 5.5 with `when.paths` listing the manifests and lockfiles above. It ships no Dockerfile, so it runs as a host subprocess with the #84 warning until #55.'''\ns=s[:j]+para+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2720,"cache_read_input_tokens":46320,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2720},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6dacfcea-81a0-4298-a939-2f0eff8ce4bf","uuid":"e8346175-b44f-4709-bc89-7b01a5c9f00c","timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:16:34.961Z","request_id":"req_011ChLEnp9aLdK5xtWBhVv8j"}
